      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>From 2001 to 2003, the total sale of bicycles B1 = 95 + 130 + 150 = 375</p>\n\n<p>From 2001 to 2003, the total sale of bicycles B2 = 184 + 200 + 216 = 600</p>\n\n<p>According to the question,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 375/600&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 62.5%</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The correct answer is 62.5%</strong></p>\n",
