    {
      "id": "0c5f7f6ee781-q22",
      "number": 22,
      "question": "Two pipes A and B can fill a tank in 20 and 30 hours, respectively. Both pipes are opened to fill the tank, but when the tank is one-third full, a leak develops through which one-fourth of the water supplied by both pipes goes out. Find the total time (in hours) taken to fill the tank.",
      "questionHtml": "Two pipes A and B can fill a tank in 20 and 30 hours, respectively. Both pipes are opened to fill the tank, but when the tank is&nbsp;one-third full, a leak develops through which one-fourth of the water supplied by both pipes goes out. Find the total time (in&nbsp;hours) taken to fill the tank.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(14 \\frac{2}{3}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(14 \\frac{2}{3}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "14",
          "html": "14"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(11 \\frac{2}{5}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(11 \\frac{2}{5}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(12 \\frac{1}{3}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(12 \\frac{1}{3}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>Rate of A = 1/20, Rate of B = 1/30, Combined rate = 1/12 tank/hour</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">Time to fill 1/3 tank = (1/3) / (1/12) = 4 hours</span></p>\n\n<p>Effective rate with leak = (3/4) × (1/12) = 1/16 tank/hour</p>\n\n<p>Time to fill remaining 2/3 tank = (2/3) / (1/16) = 32/3 hours</p>\n\n<p>Total time = 4 + (32/3) = 4 + 10<sup>2</sup>/3 = 14<sup>2</sup>/3 hours</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
